  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To accelerate the reduction of TB, Leprosy and lung disease burden through provision of people-centered, universally accessible, acceptable and affordable quality services in Kenya - Kenya (01-Jan-2018-30-Jun-2021)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kenya, Tuberculosis, Amref Health Africa (Amref Kenya)This program has the following goals: To accelerate the reduction of TB, Leprosy and lung disease burden through provision of people-centered, universally accessible, acceptable and affordable quality services in Kenya.. The objectives of this program are: Reduce new HIV infections by 75%.  Reduce AIDS related mortality by 25%.  Sustain the gains in the context of a newly devolved health system.  Intensify efforts to find &#x201c;missing&#x201d; cases.  Reduce transmission.  Prevent active disease and morbidity.  Enhance the quality of care for chronic lung diseases</narrative>
  </description>
